## 🔧 **MCP Server Configuration:**

### **Basic Setup:**
```bash
# Install and run Supabase MCP server
npx -y @supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest
```

### **Project-Scoped Mode:**
```bash
# Limit access to specific project
npx -y @supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest --project-ref=<project-ref>
```

### **Read-Only Mode (Recommended):**
```bash
# Restrict to read-only operations for security
npx -y @supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest --read-only
```

### **Feature Groups:**
```bash
# Enable specific tool groups only
npx -y @supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest --features=database,docs
```

### **Environment Variables:**
```bash
# Required for authentication
export SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN="<personal-access-token>"
```

### **MCP Client Configuration:**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "supabase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest",
        "--read-only",
        "--project-ref=<project-ref>"
      ],
      "env": {
        "SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<personal-access-token>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```